1789,"p_value":0.65723,"significant":false,"n":25},"8":{"slope_per_decade":0.04285,"p_value":0.3316,"significant":false,"n":25},"9":{"slope_per_decade":0.03995,"p_value":0.0072,"significant":true,"n":25},"10":{"slope_per_decade":0.0284,"p_value":0.27607,"significant":false,"n":25},"11":{"slope_per_decade":0.02877,"p_value":0.04713,"significant":true,"n":25},"12":{"slope_per_decade":0.02543,"p_value":0.29327,"significant":false,"n":25}},"preview_2026":{"dates":["2026-01","2026-02","2026-03","2026-04","2026-05","2026-06","2026-07"],"values":[0.46879,0.50394,0.6696,0.72514,0.7557,0.56588,0.7921],"anomaly":[0.12405,-0.01779,0.11729,0.02701,0.02577,0.01397,0.20474]},"id":"duexttau","label":"Dust optical depth (550 nm)","label_ar":"العمق البصري للغبار","unit":"","description":"How much sunlight the dust column blocks. 0.1 is clear, 0.5 is a hazy day, >1 is a dust storm month.","primary":true,"source":{"short_name":"M2TMNXAER","version":"5.12.4","variable":"DUEXTTAU","daac":"GES DISC","doi":"10.5067/FH9A0MLJPC7N","access":"power_fallback","fallback_note":"NASA POWER AOD_55: TOTAL aerosol optical depth from CERES SYN1deg, not dust-only","fallback_source":"CERES SYN1deg via NASA POWER"},"n_cells":7,"has_map":true}],"limitations":["MERRA-2 dust is a model product (reanalysis). The aerosol observations it assimilates changed over time (e.g. the end of MISR/AVHRR inputs), which can create artificial jumps. We cross-check with MODIS Deep Blue aerosol optical depth, an independent satellite record.","Optical depth measures the whole air column; surface concentration is what you breathe. They can trend differently.","Dust in Kuwait is dominated by a few big storm months each spring and summer, so annual means are noisy and trends need many years to become significant.","MODIS 1 degree cells are huge: the whole country is about two cells."],"limitations_ar":["غبار MERRA-2 ناتج نموذج إعادة تحليل؛ تغيّر الأرصاد المُدمجة قد يُحدث قفزات مصطنعة، لذلك نتحقق من MODIS.","العمق البصري يقيس عمود الهواء كله؛ التركيز السطحي هو ما تتنفسه.","يسود الغبار في الكويت في بضعة أشهر عاصفة سنوياً، لذا المتوسطات السنوية متقلبة.","خلايا MODIS بدرجة واحدة ضخمة: الكويت كلها نحو خليتين."],"verdict":{"headline":"No significant trend","headline_ar":"لا اتجاه معنوي","stamp":"INCONCLUSIVE","what":"Dust optical depth (550 nm)","where":"All Kuwait","how_much":"+0.015 per decade (95% CI -0.012 to +0.059); +0.037 in total over 2001-2025, about +7.3% versus the 2001-2010 baseline.","significant":"No. Mann-Kendall test with autocorrelation correction, p = 0.252, 25 annual values. The 95% confidence interval includes zero, so we can't tell.","what_ar":"العمق البصري للغبار","where_ar":"كل الكويت","how_much_ar":"+0.015 لكل عقد (فاصل ثقة 95%: -0.012 إلى +0.059)؛ إجمالي +0.037 خلال 2001-2025.","text":"Dust optical depth (550 nm) in All Kuwait drifted by +0.015 per decade since 2001, but the change is not statistically significant (p = 0.252). With 25 years of data we can't rule out that this is natural year-to-year variability. Note: this figure is total aerosol optical depth from NASA POWER (CERES SYN1deg), used as a labelled fallback until MERRA-2 dust-only data are fetched.","text_ar":"تغيّر العمق البصري للغبار في كل الكويت بمقدار +0.015 لكل عقد منذ 2001، لكن التغيّر ليس ذا دلالة إحصائية (p = 0.252). مع 25 سنة من البيانات لا يمكننا استبعاد أن هذا تقلّب طبيعي من سنة إلى أخرى."},"evidence":["Dust optical depth (550 nm): CERES SYN1deg via NASA POWER (FALLBACK, standing in for M2TMNXAER DUEXTTAU while Earthdata access is unavailable).","Area-weighted regional mean, monthly anomalies vs 2001-2010, annual means 2001-2025.","Trend: Mann-Kendall test with Hamed-Rao autocorrelation correction; magnitude: Sen's slope with 95% confidence interval (Theil-Sen). Seasonal Kendall on monthly anomalies as a check.","Map: per-cell Mann-Kendall + Sen's slope, Benjamini-Hochberg FDR at q = 0.05; only FDR-significant cells are drawn solid."]}